      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e Having the data structure store the last query doesn\u0027t feel quite right -- it feels like the calling class should track that. Why not have findRect() return the LocationRecord?\n\nI agree. I dislike the stateful nature of the new methods and I had initially defined it the way you suggested. That didn\u0027t sit well with me for the reason you mentioned and specifically because it opens the door to `insertFoundRect` calls with a potentially invalid `LocationRecord`. Rather than tracking the validity of `LocationRecord`s I decided for the stateful two-step procedure.\n\n\u003e That said, I\u0027m also concerned about inadvertently doing two queries in a row before trying to insert -- which *would* be an argument for keeping the last query. Then you could return false or some other error code from findRect() if there\u0027s already a LocationRecord stored. WDYT?\n\nI think that\u0027s reasonable. I wanted to allow querying for available space without making an insertion but really the only usage I have in mind is calling `findRect()`, and if it returns true, calling `insertFoundRect` without calling `findRect()` again.",
      "parentUuid": "997ac669_bd91a3fc",
      "revId": "b306f2911c6ad5d81a5c433d6288bf371e5461bd",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
